      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm, now that I\u0027ve finally figured out what `-Wassume` is doing, I think we probably want to leave it disabled. But this CL is what we would need to do to enable it. AFAICT there are no instances of `DAWN_RELEASE_ASSUME` that have side effects. So this would have no runtime effect.\n\nBasically, like `DAWN_ASSERT`, `__builtin_assume` doesn\u0027t always execute its expression. Except it _never_ executes its expression so it\u0027s even less bugprone.\n\nTentatively abandoning.",
      "revId": "999f05f177b9f02283fab6fe9004a9cb71ad8bd0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
